# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP response security headers for static hosts that read a `_headers` file
# (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages). Vite copies this file verbatim into dist/, and it
# is INERT on hosts that don't consume it (S3, Nginx, Apache) — configure the
# equivalent there (see the README "Response headers" section).
#
# This file ships the unambiguously-safe hardening headers plus the clickjacking
# control that fixes the reported cross-origin framing defect (QA Issue 19).
# `frame-ancestors` only controls who may FRAME this site, so it is safe to ship
# as-is and does NOT affect resource loading.
#
# The FULL resource-restricting Content-Security-Policy (script-src / style-src /
# img-src / font-src / frame-src …) is documented in the README and should be
# added here AFTER validating it against your deployed build, because a
# mis-scoped resource CSP can break the web font, the Google Maps embed, or the
# runtime inline styles that Framer Motion / Swiper set. When you add it, merge
# the `frame-ancestors 'self'` directive below into that single CSP header
# rather than sending two Content-Security-Policy headers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
